1
00:00:01,244 --> 00:00:12,092
This simulator proves that Moyasar accepts externally authenticated 3DS, and that a stored card can be charged later. Keys stay on the server and are hidden on screen.

2
00:00:13,697 --> 00:00:27,665
On the left is the external MPI payload, fully editable: the ECI, the authentication value, the directory server transaction ID, and the protocol version. It is passed to the provider exactly as written.

3
00:00:32,698 --> 00:00:43,882
Step one is the customer-initiated payment. The sandbox returns paid, confirms it did not run its own 3DS challenge, and returns a token for the saved card.

4
00:00:48,897 --> 00:00:56,649
Step two is the merchant-initiated charge on that token, with no shopper present, just as a subscription renewal would work.

5
00:01:03,165 --> 00:01:13,965
The full chain runs both in one click. That sandbox evidence turned an open question into a confirmed capability, and fed straight into the integration PRD.
